0361: TopazModem: the RPM's clock scaling with every bus clock held first, and a DDR manager (kern.sweet_bus_scale, default 0)

Inert unless kern.sweet_bus_scale=1 is written: with nothing written the kernel behaves as with 0360 and
0347's votes go to the RPM unchanged. Needs 0343, 0347 and 0360.

The DDR clock is the RPM's BIMC clock ("clk2" 0, key "KHz"); the RPM picks the row of the DDR plan (200,
547.2, 768, 1017.6, 1555.2, 1804.8, 2092.8 MHz) that covers the vote, but applies no rate vote until the OS
turns clock scaling on ("Enab" = 1 on "clk0" 2, as clk_smd_rpm_enable_scaling()). Nothing in this kernel did:
the DDR stays at 1555.2 MHz and votes are accepted without effect (measured with 0347). With scaling on,
each RPM bus clock is what the masters vote and one nobody votes is gated, while every consumer of this
kernel (UFS, USB, display, GPU, IPA, audio, QUP) is already running and votes none. So
kern.sweet_bus_scale=1:
1. measures the buses and the DDR (GCC debug mux inputs of debugcc-khaje.c; the DDR from mccc);
2. votes XO on in the active set (the stock keepalive);
3. holds every rate clock of khaje's table in both sets, as Linux clk_smd_rpm_handoff() (INT_MAX, or with
   kern.sweet_bus_hold=1 cnoc, snoc and mmrt at the measured rate plus 2 %);
4. holds the BIMC in both sets at the vote of the row the DDR runs at, so it does not move at the switch;
5. sends "Enab" in the sleep set, then the active set; stops at the first refusal or timeout (state -1,
   nothing changed; -2 if the active "Enab" got no good answer);
6. measures again 20 ms later and logs before -> after.
Then: kern.sweet_ddr_set=<row> moves the DDR by hand and times the switch; kern.sweet_ddr_gov=1 starts a
manager thread (every kern.sweet_ddr_gov_ms, 20) that takes the GPU's input (0347's per-level vote with
kern.sweet_gpu_ddr=1) and the CPUs' (0362), keeps the row between kern.sweet_ddr_floor and kern.sweet_ddr_cap
(1555200 and 2092800 kHz by default: never under the boot row), goes up at once and down after
kern.sweet_ddr_down_ms (100), and stays at the switch's row while any TSENS sensor is at or over
kern.sweet_ddr_temp_max (95000 m°C) until 5 C under it. kern.sweet_bus_scale=0 stops the manager and puts
the BIMC back at the switch's row; scaling stays on in the RPM (Linux never sends "Enab" 0).
kern.sweet_bus_vote, kern.sweet_bus_clocks and kern.sweet_bus_stats give a single hold, a measurement and
the state with all counters. SapphireGpu exports 0343's measurements and routes 0347's vote through the
manager. Lock order: opp_lock -> bus_lock -> rpm_lock / clk_lock.

Checked on the host (138 checks against a model of the RPM): message order of the switch, no bus under its
boot rate in either hold mode, a refused hold stops before "Enab", manager floor, cap, delay and thermal cap.
Measured on the phone (one boot for the switch): rc 0; qup 19.2 -> 200 MHz, disp_hf_axi 345 -> 417 MHz,
ipa_2x 1.5 -> 30 MHz, DDR unchanged; kern.sweet_ddr_set=1804 -> 1805054 kHz, =2092 -> 2096436 kHz, 1.65 ms per
switch, 0 votes refused. Sequential memory latency (median of 3, 4-64 MB) 6.3-7.1 -> 5.0-5.1 ns. GPU time per
Control Center animation frame (3 traces per condition, order high-low-high-manager): 15.9-16.7 ms at 2092.8
MHz, 19.4-19.8 ms at 1555.2 MHz, 17.3-17.8 ms with the manager. One boot with scaling and the manager turned
on at boot: no incident. Temperature over long runs is not measured.

